el": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2033", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2034", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2034", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2035", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2035", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2036", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2036", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2041", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2041", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2046", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2046", "type": "double"}, {"name": "accelerated_decarbonisation_2051", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "ACCELERATED DECARBONISATION 2051", "type": "double"}, {"name": "geopoint", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "geopoint", "type": "geo_point_2d"}], "dataset_id": "dfes-lv-headroom-monitored", "dataset_uid": "da_hv0mqt", "has_records": true, "features": ["analyze", "geo", "custom_view"], "attachments": [], "alternative_exports": [], "data_visible": false, "metas": {"default": {"title": "SP ENW - DFES - LV Headroom (Monitored)", "description": "<p style=\"font-family: sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; font-family: inherit;\">Dataset Classification - Open</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: inherit; font-weight: bolder;\">SP ENW</span><b style=\"font-family: inherit;\">\u00a0- DFES - LV Headroom (Monitored) Data - New 2024 Dataset</b></p>\n<p>SP ENW is currently using PreSense units to monitor the power of secondary substations, particularly those with a large number of customers. The data is processed in real-time and aggregated into half-hourly intervals. In its RIIO-ED2 Business Plan, SP ENW outlined its plans to achieve 95% network visibility coverage during the price control period using distribution monitoring equipment (PreSense),  with the remaining 5% covered by smart meters. As of March 2025, 60% of customers are covered by PreSense.\nThe substations being monitored have been identified because they have been monitored for over a year, providing sufficient data points throughout the period, especially during winter. This real-time monitoring data is used to identify the maximum demand of secondary substations. There is an ongoing programme to identify new sites for monitoring to expand coverage and improve network visibility.\n</p>\n<p>\nThis dataset contains the headroom (kVA) forecast for PreSense-monitored secondary substations, based on the maximum demand forecast and substation transformer ratings.\n</p>\n<p>\nThe collection of DFES datasets envisages a range of possible views of the future, which indicate how different influences can change electrical demand and generation on our network. \n</p>\n<p>\nThis dataset is an accompaniment to our 2024 DFES report, it contains detailed datasets and interactive tools which allow our customers to understand what our Distribution Future Electricity Scenarios mean to them.\n</p>\n<p>\nPlease refer to our main DFES report for a full description of our forecasts and scenarios. Our forecasts are not precise predictions of what the future is likely to be, but instead frame the uncertainty within our planning as explained in the main report.\n</p>\n<hr>\n<p>\nWhile we use reasonable endeavours to ensure that the data contained within this dataset is accurate, we do not accept any responsibility or liability for the accuracy or the completeness of the content held, or for any loss which may arise from reliance on this dataset and/or its related information.\n</p>\n<hr>\n<p>\nIf you have any query related to this SP ENW - DFES - LV Headroom (Monitored) Data, please contact us\u00a0\n<a href=\"mailto:dataportal@enwl.co.uk?subject=SP%20ENW%20DFES%20LV%20Headroom%20(Monitored)%20Data\">\n<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">HERE</span></a>\n</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>\n*Actual dataset content is available to registered users only \u2013 If you have not already done so, log-in or create new account below* </b></p>\n<p>\nNew User?  -  Create your new account   \n<a href=\"https://electricitynorthwest.opendatasoft.com/signup/\">\n<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">HERE</span></a>\n</p>\n<p>\nAlready registered as a SP ENW Portal User?  -  Log-In \n<a href=\"https://electricitynorthwest.opendatasoft.com/login/\">\n<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">HERE</span></a>\n</p>\n<p>\nHave you an ODS Portal account created elsewhere?  -  Log-In\n<a href=\"https://electricitynorthwest.opendatasoft.com/signup/login/\">\n<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">HERE</span></a>\n</p>\n<hr>", "theme": ["Forecasting Data"], "keyword": ["DFES", "LV", "Headroom", "Monitored", "Battery Storage Persona", "Distributed Generator Persona", "Domestic Customer Persona", "Industrial & Commercial Persona", "Local Authority Persona 1", "Local Authority Persona 2", "Network Operator Persona 1", "Network Operator Persona 2", "Small-Scale EVCP Use-Case4", "Small-Scale Renewable Use-Case"], "license": "CC BY 4.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "language": "en", "metadata_languages": ["en"], "timezone": "Europe/London", "modified": "2026-03-19T08:54:27+00:00", "modified_updates_on_metadata_change": true, "modified_updates_on_data_change": true, "data_processed": "2025-03-11T09:45:17+00:00", "metadata_processed": "2026-03-19T08:54:30.472000+00:00", "geographic_reference": ["uk_40_e92000001"], "geographic_reference_auto": true, "territory": ["England"], "geometry_types": ["Point"], "bbox": {"type": "Feature", "geometry": {"coordinates": [[[-1.8896827194839716, 54.944989518262446], [-3.5906195640563965, 54.944989518262446], [-3.5906195640563965, 53.228806955739856], [-1.8896827194839716, 53.228806955739856], [-1.8896827194839716, 54.944989518262